{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Chaincode lifecycle and deployment policies will be managed via a dedicated Lifecycle System Chaincode (LSCC) to handle both friendly name mapping and policy enforcement.",
    "The Solo orderer will be implemented as a minimal Go service using a simple in-memory slice to act as the RAM ledger, exposing a gRPC Seek API for client reconnection.",
    "The state cache will be implemented as an LRU (Least Recently Used) cache within the peer's state package to intercept read operations and speed up rw-set construction.",
    "The operator CLI will be extracted into a standalone Go binary that communicates with the peer via gRPC, removing the need for RocksDB and CGO dependencies in the CLI build process.",
    "GitHub mirroring will be handled via a CI/CD pipeline job that automatically syncs changes from the primary Gerrit repository to GitHub."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The primary development language is Go, consistent with Hyperledger Fabric.",
    "The base Hyperledger Fabric architecture (peer, orderer, chaincode container) already exists, and this increment modifies/extends it.",
    "Unit and integration tests are required for all new code and modifications.",
    "Documentation tasks involve writing Markdown files and configuring existing static site generators, not building a new website from scratch.",
    "Effort estimates include design, coding, testing, and code review preparation, but exclude deployment to production environments."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Chaincode Lifecycle & Friendly Names",
      "activity_description": "Implement updates to the lifecycle system chaincode to manage deployment policies and map friendly names to chaincode IDs for easier management and debugging (U1, U2).",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Solo Orderer Implementation",
      "activity_description": "Develop the minimal Solo ordering process, including a buffered channel for incoming writes, a single thread for block creation, an in-RAM ledger, and a Seek API for history discovery (U4).",
      "most_likely_effort": 30
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "State Cache Implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement an LRU state cache to intercept state reads, helping submitters quickly build read-write sets and improving overall peer performance (U6).",
      "most_likely_effort": 25
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Standalone Operator CLI",
      "activity_description": "Extract peer commands into a separate CLI component that communicates via gRPC, removing RocksDB and other internal peer dependencies to allow simple platform-specific binary installation (U8).",
      "most_likely_effort": 35
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "GitHub Mirroring Setup",
      "activity_description": "Configure CI/CD pipelines to automatically mirror the Hyperledger Fabric codebase from Gerrit to GitHub for public exploration (U5).",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Documentation & Website Integration",
      "activity_description": "Write documentation for chaincode upgrade flows and organize/integrate existing documentation to be easily accessible via hyperledger.org (U3, U7).",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 160
  }
}
```

